 of the real players. Each of your players looks the same every match; the other side's are drawn by their place on that night's teamsheet."}),s.jsx("li",{children:"A foul is shown where it happens: the man who fouled gets to the player on the ball, the whistle goes and the free kick is taken from that spot while he stands by it. A card shows on the foul it was given for. When a chance, a kick off or another dead ball keeps the pitch busy all through that minute, the foul is not drawn, but it is still in the list of what happened (beside the pitch on a wide screen, the latest line under the stats on a phone) and in the stats."}),s.jsx("li",{children:"Short passes roll along the grass. Long balls, crosses, throw ins, goal kicks and shots go up in the air, and the shadow under the ball shows how high."}),s.jsx("li",{children:"A goal marked (P) was a penalty. A goal marked (O.G) is an own goal: it counts for the club it is listed under, and the man named put it into his own net. On the pitch the ball goes in off him and he holds his head."}),m&&s.jsxs("li",{children:["VAR here reviews ",r&&u?"goals and penalties only":r?"goals only":"penalty calls only",", and you only see a review that changed the call.",r?" A goal that gets ruled out goes in first: the check opens with the ball in the net, the score does not move, and it adds no scorer or shot stats.":"",u?" A foul the referee missed can become a penalty, and that kick can go in, be saved or miss.":""]}),s.jsx("li",{children:"Tap one of your players to make a sub or change shape. Everything up to that minute stays. The rest of the half is played again with your change."}),s.jsx("li",{children:"Tactics from here, in the same sheet, changes your team instructions, the formation and any duty for the rest of this match only. Your standing plan stays on the Tactics tab."}),s.jsx("li",{children:"Pause, pick a speed, or Skip to the whistle. Tap a goal card to move on."})]}),s.jsxs("p",{className:"mt-2 text-xs text-foregroun